## Audit pass, and three holes in the output verifier (2026-08-18)
Read-only audit by kimi-k3-high in an isolated worktree, briefed to attack
verify-output.mjs specifically. Its shell was blocked, so it could not build or
measure; it said so up front and marked every unverifiable claim rather than
asserting it. Two of the three verifier holes came from that run.

Holes, all three confirmed by mutation against a real build:
  v1  concatenated the pages, so a refusal intact on /incidents satisfied the
      check for the same refusal truncated on /. (found earlier, by my own
      mutation test)
  v2  held a page to a string only if the page carried its first 40 chars, so
      {i.refusal.slice(38)} on / dropped that page out of the checked set while
      /incidents satisfied it. Tail truncation caught, head truncation not.
  v3  stripped <script> tags but kept their contents. A static Next export
      inlines every server-rendered string in the RSC flight payload, so
      deleting the visible breaches block left them findable in the payload.
      Confirmed in the bytes: "row count fell from 14 to 11" appears in
      out/incidents.html at offset 8929 in the DOM and 29953 inside a script.

v4 names the pages each string must appear on, discounts nesting (a refusal
quotes its own breaches, so raw fragment scanning reported every nesting as a
truncation), strips script and style contents, and bans hiding constructs
outright rather than claiming to detect them. Six mutations now caught:
head truncation, tail truncation, payload-only rendering, whole-section
deletion, disclosure hiding, seller leak.

Measured in a real browser (playwright, chromium), which the audit could not do:
  no horizontal overflow at 390/768/1280/1920, three pages, both schemes
  exactly one h1 per page
  three theme states resolve correctly, unstamped follows prefers-color-scheme
    in both directions, explicit light beats a dark OS
  skip link moves focus to #main after tabIndex={-1} was added
  --rule-strong now clears 3:1 on card/paper/sunken in both themes
    light  3.89 / 3.51 / 3.19   (was 2.77 / 2.50 / 2.27)
    dark   3.59 / 3.89 / 3.25   (was 2.67 / 2.89 / 2.41)
  the audit's hand-computed contrast matched the browser to 2dp

